[thin] These closest approaches occur where the S25R parking blocks meet the receiver's top and at the edge of the 0.45 mm high cut-edge pad. They are terminating boundaries of stock backed by the receiver or the adjoining 2.85 mm upright; the cover parks by gravity at its source cut edge. They are not a thin functional snap catch. The parking feature's handling force is unmeasured.
alternatives: Extending the parking blocks into a larger solid buttress adds backing without changing the source cover, but occupies more of the open cut-edge access. A taller pad needs the parked cover translated and its neighboring clearance rechecked. A separate large parking tray avoids the local pads with a larger footprint and one more part.
