[thin] These are the rounded receiver side stock and end-cap boundaries around the fixed wing channel, not the clearance being varied. The outer width is 30.80 mm and wing-channel width 24.80 mm, giving 3.00 mm nominal straight side stock; the R2 outer corners produce the shorter local readings near the rounded ends. Other picks approach the 3.00 mm top cap obliquely toward a marking or inspection-window edge. No load or handling-life result is inferred.
alternatives: Widening the receiver by 2.00 mm gives 4.00 mm nominal straight side stock while preserving the channel, but increases the occupied width of all five lanes on their 34 mm pitch. Square outer corners add material at these minima but replace the rounded handling corners. Closing or lengthening the end caps adds stock at their edges but reduces the inspection/removal opening.
