[ledge] These small horizontal underside faces belong to the added S25R source-cover parking saddles, above Z 10.05 and outside the open sliding channel. They retain the relaxed cover's cut-edge parking pose. The prepared kit keeps automatic supports, with the underside and outboard sides accessible for removal; the finished parking surfaces remain unprinted.
alternatives: Solid buttresses continuing down to the bed eliminate these small print-down faces but fill the outboard access below the cut-edge saddles. Tapered undersides reduce support demand but need a new cover parking/handling clearance review. A separate open tray removes the overhang from the receiver at the cost of another part and more footprint.
